<title>FRANCE: TENNIS-FRENCH OPEN DOUBLES RESULTS.</title>
<headline>TENNIS-FRENCH OPEN DOUBLES RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-05-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Doubles results on the sixth day of</p>
<p>the French Open tennis championships on Saturday (prefix number</p>
<p>denotes seeding):</p>
<p>Mixed doubles, first round</p>
<p>Patricia Tarabini/Javier Frana (Argentina) beat Katrina</p>
<p>Adams/Mark Keil (U.S.) 6-4 6-1</p>
<p>Alexia Dechaume-Balleret/Jean-Philippe Fleurian (France) beat</p>
<p>Anne-Gaelle Sidot/Lionel Roux (France) 7-6 (7-5) 6-4</p>
<p>Florencia Labat (Argentina)/Andrew Kratzmann (Australia) beat</p>
<p>Nicole Arendt/Luke Jensen (U.S.) 3-6 7-6 (7-5) 8-6</p>
<p>Second round</p>
<p>Ruxandra Dragomir (Romania)/Leander Paes (India) beat 14-Elena</p>
<p>Likhovtseva (Russia)/Jeff Tarango (U.S.) 7-6 (10-8) 6-4</p>
<p>15-Mercedes Paz/Pablo Albano (Argentina) beat Helena Vildova</p>
<p>(Czech Republic)/Filippo Messori (Italy) 6-3 7-5</p>
<p>Barbara Rittner/Karsten Braasch (Germany) beat 2-Larisa Neiland</p>
<p>(Latvia)/Andrei Olhovskiy (Russia) 6-3 7-6 (7-2)</p>
<p>6-Alexandra Fusai (France)/David Adams (South Africa) beat</p>
<p>Magalie Lamarre/Olivier Delaitre (France) 7-5 6-2</p>
<p>8-Debbie Graham (U.S.)/Ellis Ferreira (South Africa) beat Laura</p>
<p>Montalvo/Lucas Arnold (Argentina) 6-4 6-4</p>
<p>7-Brenda Schultz-McCarthy (Netherlands)/Piet Norval (South</p>
<p>Africa) beat Yayuk Basuki (Indonesia)/Tom Nijssen (Netherlands)</p>
<p>6-3 7-5</p>
<p>1-Lisa Raymond/Patrick Galbraith (U.S.) beat Karine</p>
<p>Quentrec-Eagle/Rodolphe Gilbert (France) 4-6 6-2 6-3</p>
<p>Rachel McQuillan/David MacPherson (Australia) beat 5-Caroline</p>
<p>Vis (Netherlands)/Byron Talbot (South Africa)</p>
<p>6-4 7-5</p>
<p>Kathy Rinaldi-Stunkel/Trevor Kronemann (U.S.) beat 11-Kristie</p>
<p>Boogert/Menno Oosting (Netherlands) 4-6 6-3 6-4</p>
<p>13-Miriam Oremans/Hendrik Jan Davids (Netherlands) beat Louise</p>
<p>Pleming (Australia)/Neil Broad (Britain) 6-4 4-6 6-4</p>
<p>16-Rika Hiraki (Japan)/Mahesh Bhupathi (India) beat Kristine</p>
<p>Kunce (Australia)/Scott Davis (U.S.) 2-6 6-2 9-7</p>
<p>4-Helena Sukova/Cyril Suk (Czech Republic) beat Kimberly Po</p>
<p>(U.S.)/Rikard Bergh (Sweden) 6-3 4-6 6-2</p>
<p>Men's doubles, second round</p>
<p>Tom Kempers/Menno Oosting (Netherlands) beat 9-Jonas</p>
<p>Bjorkman/Nicklas Kulti (Sweden) 6-3 1-6 6-3</p>
<p>2-Jacco Eltingh/Paul Haarhuis (Netherlands) beat Pat Cash</p>
<p>(Australia)/Richey Reneberg (U.S.) 3-6 6-1 6-4</p>
<p>7-Rick Leach/Jonathan Stark (U.S.) beat Gustavo</p>
<p>Kuerten/Fernando Meligeni (Brazil) 6-3 6-3</p>
<p>Sander Groen/Jan Siemerink (Netherlands) beat Mahesh</p>
<p>Bhupathi/Leander Paes (India) 6-7 (5-7) 7-6 (7-5) 6-3</p>
<p>Lucas Arnold/Daniel Orsanic (Argentina) beat 5-Sebastien Lareau</p>
<p>(Canada)/Alex O'brien (U.S.) 7-6 (8-6) 4-6 6-1</p>
<p>4-Yevgeny Kafelnikov (Russia)/Daniel Vacek (Czech Republic)</p>
<p>beat Tom Nijssen/Stephen Noteboom (Netherlands) 6-1 6-4</p>
<p>Women's doubles, second round</p>
<p>Mercedes Paz (Argentina)/Rene Simpson (Canada) beat 9-Katrina</p>
<p>Adams/Lori McNeil (U.S.) 6-4 6-3</p>
<p>2-Lindsay Davenport (U.S.)/Jana Novotna (Czech Republic) beat</p>
<p>Anke Huber (Germany)/Monica Seles (U.S.) 7-5 7-6</p>
<p>(7-3)</p>
<p>6-Nicole Arendt (U.S.)/Manon Bollegraf (Netherlands) beat</p>
<p>Emilie Loit/Amelie Mauresmo (France) 3-6 6-3 9-7</p>
<p>7-Yayuk Basuki (Indonesia)/Caroline Vis (Netherlands) beat Ines</p>
<p>Gorrochategui (Argentina)/Linda Wild (U.S.) 6-3 6-3</p>
<p>11-Naoko Kijimuta/Nana Miyagi (Japan) beat Virag Csurgo</p>
<p>(Hungary)/Liezel Horn (South Africa) 6-3 6-3</p>
<p>16-Ruxandra Dragomir (Romania)/Iva Majoli (Croatia) beat</p>
<p>Wiltrud Probst (Germany)/Ai Sugiyama (Japan) 5-7 6-4 6-2</p>
